<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "https://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	Listener is signed with the hardened runtime and requires no entitlements.

	It is a statically linked Go binary that only links Apple system frameworks
	(Cocoa, CoreGraphics, ApplicationServices, and OpenGL via Fyne/GLFW). It does
	not JIT, does not load third-party dylibs at runtime, and does not need a
	debugger attached.

	Do not add hardened-runtime exceptions here without a concrete, demonstrated
	need. This process holds an Accessibility TCC grant, so it can synthesise
	input across the entire system. Exceptions such as get-task-allow,
	allow-dyld-environment-variables, disable-library-validation,
	allow-unsigned-executable-memory and disable-executable-page-protection each
	turn that grant into a local privilege-escalation path: they let another
	local process attach to, inject into, or replace code inside a binary that
	can type on the user's behalf.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
	<dict/>
</plist>
